WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.631
Week 16: Weather, Nature, and Plans. understand a forecast describe terrain change plans because of conditions

2
00:00:07.631 --> 00:00:15.071
Cultural lens. Climate diversity from the Caribbean to Patagonia; ecological tourism and risk.

3
00:00:15.071 --> 00:00:27.142
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:27.142 --> 00:00:39.000
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:47.999
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:47.999 --> 00:01:16.327
Model language. Mañana va a llover en la costa. — It is going to rain on the coast tomorrow. Hace viento en las zonas altas. — It is windy in the highlands. Si cambia el tiempo, regresamos temprano. — If the weather changes, we will return early. Se prohíbe encender fuego en el bosque. — Lighting fires in the forest is prohibited. Estamos protegiendo una fuente de agua. — We are protecting a water source.

7
00:01:16.327 --> 00:01:26.246
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
